# Template for /etc/remote-access/remote.env, the host-local settings of reverse-tunnel@.service and
# sshx.service. The real values stay off this public repo: the publish URL works like a password, as
# anyone who has it can post a link there. Create the real file as root, mode 0600 (systemd reads it
# as root), with the values the old /etc/rc.local lines used. See deploy/README.md.

# The `user@host` argument and the `-p` port of the old autossh lines.
TUNNEL_REMOTE_LOGIN="tunnel-user@tunnel-host.example"
TUNNEL_REMOTE_PORT="22"

# The URL the old sshx line POSTed the session link to (`curl "<this>" -d "$line"`).
SSHX_PUBLISH_URL="https://publish-host.example/deploy/sshx-<id>/ubuntu"
